Z||000001||Old Lar||12-13-2001||02:02 PM||||When Tri State Fiero Club was around, there used to be meetings in NJ at Cubby's drive in. (good ribs) I made the trip a couple of times.  There is no formal New York State Fiero club that I know of.  There was an informal Fiero group near Owego NY, but every scheduled gathering this past year was at a time when I could't make it. ||||reg||9
Z||000002||kneebarx||12-13-2001||02:51 PM||||Aw man, that sucks, just when I'm about to get my first fiero back from the dead too!<BR>Maybe someone should start one up again, it stinks that all the fiero ppl live like in michigan and ohio and cali.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||12-13-2001||04:53 PM||||Well there is Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Association (MAFOA)<P>Fiero Owners Club of New England (FOCONE)<P>Long Island Fiero Enthusiasts (LIFE)<P>New England Fiero Association (NEFA)<P>None of them are close to me, but I belong to 3 of the 4 mentioned and go to their events, all of which are a several hours drive away.  The nice part is I get to drive to them in my Fiero.||||reg||1
